# Canvas Intent View Governance

Read this rule before adding or modifying intent-triggered views, overlay panels, or idle canvas surfaces.

## Full-Canvas Takeover (Non-Negotiable)

- Intent views (triggered by chips, voice commands, or system menu items) render at **100% W x 100% H** of the canvas content zone (`absolute inset-0` within the content flex child).
- When an intent view is active (`activeExperience` is set), ALL idle chrome MUST be hidden: `PlatformIdleGlassPanel`, `ShellIntentChips`, `OSMenuList`, accordion cards, helper text.
- No split views. No half-cards. No `max-w-2xl` constraints on intent overlays.
- Each intent view provides a single close/back affordance (top-left, `ICON_SIZES.canvasControl` from `brand.ts`).

## No Duplicate Control Surfaces

- If a control exists in the system menu (`useSystemMenuAuthority`), it MUST NOT also appear as an accordion card, details element, or persistent widget on the idle canvas.
- The idle canvas shows intent chips and the OS menu list. Detailed configuration UIs belong inside intent views or the system menu overlay — not both.

## Prohibited Patterns

| Pattern | Violation |
|---------|-----------|
| `<details>` accordion on idle canvas duplicating a system menu item | `duplicate_control_surface` |
| Intent view with `max-w-2xl` or similar width constraint | `intent_view_not_fullscreen` |
| Idle chrome visible while `activeExperience` is set | `idle_chrome_leak` |
| Intent view without close/back button | `missing_view_dismiss` |
